/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:420:      "docstring": "Fill partitioned regions with concentric colored bands derived from marker pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- Grid partitioned into regions by wall-colored lines.\n- Each region has a dominant base color and a few isolated marker pixels of other colors at varying depths from the region boundary.\n\nRule:\n- For each region, read marker colors ordered by their Chebyshev distance from the boundary to build a color palette.\n- If no marker sits on the boundary itself, the base color leads the palette.\n- Paint every cell with palette[distance mod palette_length], producing repeating concentric rectangular frames that radiate inward.\n\nKey insight: Each marker's depth from the boundary defines its position in the cyclic palette; the pattern then tiles inward automatically.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:444:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:453:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:522:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:610:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:875:      "docstring": "Fill periodic progressions that shoot from a unique grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.  Sparse non-bg dots of several colors.\n- All repeating colors originate from the same grid edge (top, bottom,\n  left, or right — the one with the most non-bg dots).\n- Each repeating color has exactly 2 dots per shooting-direction line;\n  their gap defines the step.\n- Every non-bg dot lies on a shooting-direction line that contains a\n  repeating color.\n\nRule:\n- Determine the unique shooting edge; left/right → rows, top/bottom → columns.\n- For each shooting-direction line, the repeating color has exactly 2 dots;\n  step = gap between them, offset = first position mod step.\n- A different-colored dot aligned to the same beat (pos % step == offset) is\n  a companion: it absorbs the ray and becomes the fill color, limiting the\n  fill range to the span between repeating and companion dots.\n- An unaligned dot is a bystander and left untouched.\n- Without a companion the repeating color fills the entire line.\n\nKey insight: the shooting edge is identified by counting boundary dots;\nthe gap between the two marker dots is the period; a companion sharing the\nmodular class acts as a wall that stops the ray and dictates the paint color.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:883:        "transform": "fill background/marker cells on that path with the trajectory color; ties apply both row and column rules"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:893:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:976:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:1158:      "docstring": "Simulate particles along a path with alternating turn direction at collisions.\n\nInput structure:\n- Top-left: 2x2 monochrome blocks define a repeating color cycle (left-to-right).\n- Isolated single pixels of a cycle color: start markers adjacent to the path.\n- A 2x2 monochrome block of a distinct color: end marker.\n\nRule:\n- Each start marker launches a particle moving straight, painting cycle colors in order.\n- On hitting a boundary, paint that cell with the end color and turn 90°.\n- Turn direction alternates: odd collisions → left (CCW), even → right (CW).\n- If the scheduled turn is blocked, the particle stops.\n\nKey insight: The alternating left/right turn rule is the core mechanism; without it the path would be trivial.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:1162:        "src": "start markers: isolated single pixels whose colors belong to a template cycle shown as 2x2 monochrome blocks in the top-left",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:1166:        "transform": "erase the template 2x2 blocks and the 2x2 end block; while moving, recolor visited path cells by the cycle; on collision into template background, paint that collided cell with the end-block color as a corner marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:1168:        "notes": "initial direction is the first adjacent path neighbor in priority R,D,L,U; cycle index starts at the marker’s own color within the cycle; apply independently for each marker"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:1183:        "object:marker",
