/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5052:      "docstring": "Replicate a pre-drawn corner pattern to every other marker-bearing corner.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most frequent color. Hollow 0-frames (possibly partial L-shapes); each\n  frame-corner cell is either 0 or a painted (non-bg, non-0) color.\n- >= 1 'source' corner: the pattern is already drawn (one color, both outward\n  cells and an inward-diagonal trail).\n- Other corners: a single colored pixel on the inward diagonal at the pattern's\n  deepest (k,k) offset; the pixel's color is that corner's target color.\n\nRule:\n- Extract the canonical (TL-oriented) pattern from any source.\n- For each non-source corner whose marker cell is colored, paint the same\n  pattern rotated to that corner's orientation, using the marker's color.\n\nKey insight: the pattern is symmetric about the corner's inward-diagonal axis\n(canonical dr == dc), so it reflects cleanly across all four corner orientations.\nPainting uses each target's OWN marker color, not the source color.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5084:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5157:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5418:      "docstring": "Extend marker tiles outward from '+' shapes by repeating them to the grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- A dominant non-bg color forms several '+'-shaped objects.\n- Small colored patches (1–few cells) sit adjacent to each arm of a '+'.\n\nRule:\n- For each marker tile touching a '+', determine which side of the '+' it sits on.\n- Project the tile away from the '+' in that direction, repeating the tile pattern periodically until the grid boundary.\n- '+' pixels are never overwritten.\n\nKey insight: Each marker's attachment side determines its extension direction; the pattern repeats periodically, not as a single copy.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5422:        "src": "marker tile (non-bg patch) attached to a '+' sprite",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5423:        "path": "straight ray starting from the marker tile, going away from the '+' attachment side until boundary",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5424:        "trajectory": "repeat the marker tile periodically along the ray (tile repeats every tile width/height)",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5426:        "transform": "copy the repeated marker pattern into background; keep the '+' pixels unchanged"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5437:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5492:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5556:      "docstring": "Move a triangular sprite across the grid, consuming aligned marker pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- Frames concatenated horizontally with solid divider columns; bg is most common color.\n- Each frame: a triangular arrow-shaped sprite and scattered single-pixel markers, all one color.\n\nRule:\n- Start from the rightmost frame.\n- At each step, exactly one cardinal direction from the head has reachable\n  markers (on a half-line: same row or column); the sprite advances to the\n  nearest one.\n- On reaching a marker, consume it; sprite re-faces that direction.\n- Repeat until no markers remain; output the final sprite position on a clean bg.\n\nKey insight: The triangle's tip encodes facing direction, which sets marker-consumption priority.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5559:        "summary": "A triangular sprite moves through the grid consuming scattered marker pixels that match its head orientation, turning only when matching a marker, until all markers are consumed.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5562:        "dst": "scattered single-pixel markers of same color d",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5569:        "multi_step": "Step 1: identify triangular sprite and all scattered markers in each frame; Step 2: sprite moves toward marker aligned with head direction; Step 3: consume marker and optionally turn 90° toward next aligned marker; Step 4: repeat until all markers consumed; Step 5: output shows sprite at final position with remaining markers removed",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5573:          "marker-consumption",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5580:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5586:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5660:        "marker",
