/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:8598:      "docstring": "Mirror colored sprites using red (2) markers as reflection axes.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Red (2) = marker color.\n- Colored sprites appear near red markers.\n\nRule:\n- Red line within a sprite (vertical or horizontal) → mirror payload across that axis.\n- Single red pixel in a mixed sprite → point-reflect payload around it.\n- Isolated red pixel (alone, no payload) → point-reflect each adjacent 8-connected color component.\n- Originals remain; mirrored pixels overlay.\n\nKey insight: Red marker geometry (line vs single pixel) determines reflection type; isolated vs embedded red determines what gets reflected.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:8602:        "src": "colored sprites s + red marker pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:8603:        "transform": "mirror s across the red marker axis (vertical/horizontal red line) or point-reflect around an isolated red pixel; paint the mirrored pixels onto bg"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:8607:        "catalog:marker_axis",
