/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:10243:      "docstring": "Paint an inner border around the region reachable from a corner marker pixel.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color; wall color (blue) forms barriers dividing the grid.\n- A unique single pixel (magenta) sits on one corner — the start marker.\n- Some wall-colored pixels are structural (border-touching, enclosing regions); others are decorations.\n\nRule:\n- Flood-fill from the marker corner to find all reachable bg cells, blocked by structural walls.\n- Erase wall-colored decorations hidden behind structural walls (not reachable from marker side).\n- Paint orange (color 7) on every reachable bg cell adjacent to a wall or grid edge — forming a 1-cell inner border.\n\nKey insight: Only border-connected wall components act as real barriers; interior wall fragments are decorations to be removed.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:10278:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:10340:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:10404:      "docstring": "Fill rectangles between diagonal marker pairs using a color legend.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg grid with a vertical legend at the bottom-left: each row is a (marker_color, fill_color) pair.\n- Scattered L-shaped corner markers of each marker color define opposite corners of axis-aligned rectangles.\n- Some markers are solid 2×2 blocks instead of corner pairs.\n\nRule:\n- Read legend bottom-to-top; for each entry find all pixels of that marker color.\n- Determine which two bbox corners carry L-shaped anchors — the *other* diagonal defines the fill region.\n- Fill the diamond (all shortest-path cells between those two corners) with the legend's fill color.\n- Solid 2×2 marker blocks are simply recolored to the fill color.\n- Later legend entries are protected from earlier fills.\n\nKey insight: The L-shaped anchors sit on the marker diagonal; the fill goes on the opposite diagonal of the bounding box.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:10407:        "summary": "Use a color legend at bottom-left to find diagonal marker pairs of matching color, then fill the rectangle between them with the adjacent legend color.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:10415:        "symbol_instructions": "legend is vertical stack of color pairs at bottom-left, each pair (left-right only) has marker color on left and fill color on right",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:10416:        "multi_step": "Step 1: identify legend as vertically stacked color pairs at bottom-left corner; Step 2: process legend entries from bottom to top; Step 3: for each legend entry (marker_color on left, fill_color on right), find all diagonal pairs of marker_color pixels; Step 4: fill rectangle between each diagonal pair with fill_color",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:10419:          "diagonal-markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:10434:        "object:marker",
